scout master of troop 209 and Northwest Suburban Council,

13
00:01:27,240 --> 00:01:30,280
And he wrote in to say: Clark, I just wanted to drop you a line of thanks.

14
00:01:30,320 --> 00:01:32,800
Your words frequently speak to me in the needs of our scouts.

15
00:01:32,800 --> 00:01:36,600
They're often shared among leaders of our troop and council, often affirming

16
00:01:36,600 --> 00:01:40,759
what we know, occasionally challenged what we think, but they're always appreciated.

17
00:01:40,759 --> 00:01:41,720
Keep up the good work.

18
00:01:41,720 --> 00:01:45,800
If you're ever in the Chicagoland area, we would be delighted to share a

19
00:01:45,800 --> 00:01:48,039
campfire with you anytime and show our thanks.

20
00:01:48,039 --> 00:01:49,520
Well, thanks so much, Bruce,

21
00:01:49,920 --> 00:01:51,320
Thanks for your kind words-

22
00:01:51,320 --> 00:01:54,759
They always mean a lot- and thanks for being in touch.

23
00:01:55,080 --> 00:01:57,360
Over on Google plus, Robert Slike shared this.

24
00:01:57,360 --> 00:01:59,680
He said we had a fantastic troop meeting the other night.

25
00:02:00,280 --> 00:02:06,360
My boys followed the instructions put out by scoutmastercgcom on how to set up patrols.

26
00:02:06,480 --> 00:02:10,080
We had leadership elections and I have a new cadre of youth leaders

27
00:02:10,080 --> 00:02:12,280
from the top on down and I'm looking forward to it.

28
00:02:12,560 --> 00:02:16,120
And Robert is a scout master for a troop down in Fort Bragg.

29
00:02:16,560 --> 00:02:21,280
Thanks so much, Robert, and I'm glad you were able to put it to work for your troop.

30
00:02:21,920 --> 00:02:28,040
Heard from Mike, who's an assistant scout master of troop 1434 in Potomac, Maryland.

31
00:02:28,040 --> 00:02:30,520
He said I promoted your website and Frank

32
00:02:30,520 --> 00:02:35,960
Marinard's blog, Bob White Blather and the Brian on scouting blog and ask Andy

33
00:02:35,960 --> 00:02:41,200
column on the net commission during my second week of wood badge training.

34
00:02:41,560 --> 00:02:45,000
I remain surprised by how committed scouts are thrilled to learn

35
00:02:45,000 --> 00:02:48,040
of these great resources since they haven't yet come across them.

36
00:02:48,440 --> 00:02:50,680
Well, those are some key things

37
00:02:50,680 --> 00:02:55,000
I'll tell you. Frank Marinards blog, Bob White Blather, is written

38
00:02:55,000 --> 00:02:57,960
from the standpoint of Frank being a committee chair.

39
00:02:58,160 --> 00:03:02,720
He's got excellent information on there, something that you definitely want to check out.

40
00:03:02,960 --> 00:03:08,720
Brian on scouting: that's the official blog, I believe of scouting magazine right

41
00:03:09,240 --> 00:03:13,480
And always good, up to date information on what's going on with Boy Scouts

42
00:03:13,480 --> 00:03:18,160
from America and ask Andy. if you haven't found, ask Andy.

43
00:03:18,160 --> 00:03:20,040
Well, you must rush right over there

44
00:03:20,280 --> 00:03:22,840
And he's on the US scouting service project.

45
00:03:22,840 --> 00:03:28,920
They are really good resources and, Mike, I am honored to be counted amongst them.

46
00:03:28,920 --> 00:03:33,720
Thank you very much. Another Mike, Michael Gros of Crestline,

47
00:03:33,720 --> 00:03:37,359
California, wrote in to say this: I have recently discovered your podcast.

48
00:03:37,359 --> 00:03:40,720
I'm currently going through the archives and have enjoyed the information

49
00:03:40,720 --> 00:03:42,600
and the relaxed, friendly format.

50
00:03:42,600 --> 00:03:45,600
I'm volunteering at Forest Lawn Scout Reservation.

51
00:03:45,840 --> 00:03:50,600
I'd like to get permission to broadcast your podcast on our camp radio station.

52
00:03:50,600 --> 00:03:55,799
Well, of course you can, Mike, use this podcast and all the other information

53
00:03:55,799 --> 00:03:58,400
you find at ScoutmasterCGcom freely.

54
00:03:58,840 --> 00:04:04,359
If it can help, if it can support scouting in any way, you go on ahead and use it.

55
00:04:04,400 --> 00:04:08,959
And if you go down to the bottom of the page

56
00:04:09,359 --> 00:04:14,320
on any page at ScoutmasterCGcom, you'll see the little Creative Commons license thing.

57
00:04:14,519 --> 00:04:18,040
It doesn't have many things in the way of restriction and sharing,

58
00:04:18,040 --> 00:04:24,120
It's just. I guess what it's called is a attribution no alteration kind of thing

59
00:04:24,159 --> 00:04:29,080
Where so long as you attribute the work to me and so long as you don't alter it.

60
00:04:29,120 --> 00:04:31,159
share it all you want. That's fine.

61
00:04:31,159 --> 00:04:35,840
And good friend of the blog and the podcast, Bill Daniel,

62
00:04:36,200 --> 00:04:41,920
Scoutmaster from Troop 132, responded to a post that I put out recently.

63
00:04:42,360 --> 00:04:44,320
He says: thank you for your service to scouting.

64
00:04:44,680 --> 00:04:49,480
You've posted about a divisive subject and naturally we're not going to solve it

65
00:04:49,480 --> 00:04:53,240
over the blog. And Bill goes on to ask this interesting question.

66
00:04:53,240 --> 00:04:57,000
He says: should we avoid it in this community of scouts that you and other

67
00:04:57,000 --> 00:05:00,880
contributors have created, or be divided or be distracted?

68
00:05:01,480 --> 00:05:05,400
This blog and podcast has the effect of approving the hands-on impact

69
00:05:05,400 --> 00:05:08,600
of scouts in scouts lives. every week

70
00:05:08,600 --> 00:05:10,560
Its circle of influence is expanding.

71
00:05:11,240 --> 00:05:12,280
Troops are improving.

72
00:05:12,280 --> 00:05:17,000
Scouts are growing in their ability to help scouts develop through the methods

73
00:05:17,000 --> 00:05:19,720
of the program. I encourage you to stay the course,

74
00:05:19,720 --> 00:05:23,120
unify and keep encouraging adults to trust the program because it works

75
00:05:23,120 --> 00:05:25,760
Well. Bill, I really do appreciate that.

76
00:05:25,760 --> 00:05:30,400
Now I am going to uncharacteristically and just for a moment,

77
00:05:30,720 --> 00:05:34,000
go into this area of debatable questions for a moment.

78
00:05:34,240 --> 00:05:38,160
A lot of us have been talking and have been distracted and potentially

79
00:05:38,160 --> 00:05:40,120
divided by the news in recent weeks.

80
00:05:41,240 --> 00:05:42,880
These are kind of divisive times.

81
00:05:43,280 --> 00:05:46,720
We're in the midst of a hotly contested presidential election.

82
00:05:47,200 --> 00:05:50,960
The Boy Scouts of America is working through some major controversies

83
00:05:50,960 --> 00:05:55,440
over past practices and reporting child abuse and in challenges

84
00:05:55,440 --> 00:05:58,760
to excluding gay leaders and now, apparently, scouts,

85
00:05:59,160 --> 00:06:01,160
And this is getting a lot of airtime.

86
00:06:01,160 --> 00:06:05,880
These are touchy issues to talk about, but I want to offer my

87
00:06:05,880 --> 00:06:08,560
thoughts because I think the airways are full of stories

88
00:06:08,880 --> 00:06:12,600
And I know that a lot of us are feeling unsettled- and I mean us.

89
00:06:13,080 --> 00:06:14,200
It's unsettling.

90
00:06:14,200 --> 00:06:16,960
I don't know that it's a good idea for me to pass judgment on

91
00:06:16,960 --> 00:06:20,080
or discuss the BSA's membership policies, because as soon as we open

92
00:06:20,080 --> 00:06:22,360
that door, that's all we're going to be talking about

93
00:06:22,760 --> 00:06:27,840
And there are going to be points about which good people can disagree,

94
00:06:28,560 --> 00:06:31,240
just like politics and just like religion.

95
00:06:31,440 --> 00:06:35,159
OK, And that's why we don't discuss them in detail here,

96
00:06:35,360 --> 00:06:38,600
because they distract us from serving our scouts.

97
00:06:39,000 --> 00:06:41,840
For a moment, let's lay all those things aside

98
00:06:42,160 --> 00:06:45,440
and think about scouting beyond the context of organizations

99
00:06:45,440 --> 00:06:48,320
and personalities and see it as its founder did,

100
00:06:48,880 --> 00:06:52,960
because Baden Powell and vision. scouting is a vehicle for bringing peace to the world.

101
00:06:53,400 --> 00:06:55,680
because of this vision, over the last century,

102
00:06:55,680 --> 00:06:59,320
Scouting has found a home in many, many places in the world.

103
00:06:59,960 --> 00:07:02,880
We reverence and respect different expressions of religions,

104
00:07:02,880 --> 00:07:07,480
politics, nationality and culture and, beyond simply tolerating those differences,

105
00:07:07,480 --> 00:07:08,920
We accept that they're our strength.

106
00:07:08,920 --> 00:07:11,000
We accept that diversity is important.

107
00:07:11,320 --> 00:07:16,440
You know, last summer, high in the Bernie's Alps, in Condorsteg, Switzerland,

108
00:07:16,719 --> 00:07:19,680
I had the great pleasure of sitting around a campfire with our fellow scouts

109
00:07:19,680 --> 00:07:24,320
from Portugal and we had a wonderful evening. just you know, being scouts,

110
00:07:24,800 --> 00:07:29,520
We shared some kitchen space and an eating area with scouts from Great Britain.

111
00:07:29,520 --> 00:07:32,640
We spent time with scouts from Switzerland, of course,

112
00:07:32,640 --> 00:07:37,840
in Brazil and Mauritius and Russia and Kenya and Greece and many other places,

113
00:07:38,599 --> 00:07:40,719
And we couldn't all speak the same language,

114
00:07:41,719 --> 00:07:43,880
We didn't all worship the same God,

115
00:07:43,880 --> 00:07:47,520
We didn't share the same political opinions, but we came together,

116
00:07:47,960 --> 00:07:51,039
having a whole lot in common, just because we were scouts,

117
00:07:51,599 --> 00:07:53,280
And that's the heart of the movement.

118
00:07:53,280 --> 00:07:58,919
So our scouting movement is bigger than political or religious or moral dogma.

119
00:07:59,400 --> 00:08:02,880
Scouting is a simple expression of values common to every enlightened

120
00:08:02,880 --> 00:08:04,880
society throughout human history.

121
00:08:05,240 --> 00:08:07,400
These values aren't anything new.

122
00:08:07,400 --> 00:08:11,080
They're too broad to be owned by any one religious or political

123
00:08:11,080 --> 00:08:13,280
or organizational point of view.

124
00:08:13,280 --> 00:08:15,200
Each scout judges their own heart.

125
00:08:15,920 --> 00:08:18,720
We look on our fellow scouts as we hope they look on us

126
00:08:18,720 --> 00:08:22,120
with understanding and acceptance and tolerance.

127
00:08:22,920 --> 00:08:26,880
The genius of scouting is that we look beyond differences

128
00:08:27,320 --> 00:08:29,480
to what we hold in common.

129
00:08:29,480 --> 00:08:31,360
Now, division is easy,

130
00:08:31,360 --> 00:08:34,480
Division is cheap and division is cowardly.

131
00:08:35,320 --> 00:08:39,480
And when people try to divide us on matters of politics,

132
00:08:39,880 --> 00:08:43,439
on matters of religion, on matters of custom and culture,

133
00:08:44,120 --> 00:08:45,720
it's an easy job.

134
00:08:45,720 --> 00:08:47,640
Unity is what takes a lot of work.

135
00:08:47,640 --> 00:08:52,680
Unity requires us to accommodate charitably those with whom we disagree.

136
00:08:53,000 --> 00:08:56,240
It requires us to bravely share our world and ourselves

137
00:08:56,280 --> 00:08:58,280
with those who disagree with us.

138
00:08:59,080 --> 00:09:02,680
Organizations and religions and political parties. they're pretty inflexible,

139
00:09:02,840 --> 00:09:05,600
They're slow to change, but they do eventually.

140
00:09:06,080 --> 00:09:09,000
They're bound by rules and policies and traditions.

141
00:09:09,360 --> 00:09:11,840
They're inherently intolerant and insular.

142
00:09:12,160 --> 00:09:14,040
They're kind of tribal

143
00:09:14,040 --> 00:09:16,520
And these sound like bad things.

144
00:09:17,520 --> 00:09:20,400
But all I'm doing is this is just observational.

145
00:09:20,400 --> 00:09:24,920
OK, don't see this as a negative judgment about the nature of organizations.

146
00:09:25,079 --> 00:09:27,680
I'm just observing that this is generally true.

147
00:09:27,920 --> 00:09:31,760
Maybe the next great leap of humanity will come when we finally do away

148
00:09:31,760 --> 00:09:34,560
with all the pettiness and divisions of tribalism

149
00:09:35,000 --> 00:09:36,839
and embrace the common good in each other.

150
00:09:36,839 --> 00:09:41,120
And I'll bet scouting will have a big part in that.

151
00:09:41,479 --> 00:09:43,760
What did our founder say?

152
00:09:43,760 --> 00:09:47,120
What did the guy who put all this together have to tell us?

153
00:09:47,479 --> 00:09:52,839
Well, Beaton Powell, in his last message to scout leaders, said:

154
00:09:53,040 --> 00:09:56,560
our aim is to produce healthy, happy, helpful citizens,

155
00:09:57,200 --> 00:10:00,200
to eradicate the prevailing narrow self interest:

156
00:10:00,760 --> 00:10:03,800
personal, political, sectarian and national,

157
00:10:04,320 --> 00:10:08,560
and to substitute for it a broader spirit of self sacrifice

158
00:10:08,560 --> 00:10:11,160
and service in the cause of humanity,

159
00:10:11,160 --> 00:10:14,560
and thus to develop mutual goodwill and cooperation,

160
00:10:14,560 --> 00:10:19,440
not only within our own country but abroad, between all countries.

161
00:10:20,360 --> 00:10:25,800
Experience shows that this consummation is no idle or fantastic dream,

162
00:10:26,360 --> 00:10:29,600
but is a practical possibility if we work for it.

163
00:10:30,680 --> 00:10:35,080
Therefore, you, you scout leaders, are not only doing a great work

164
00:10:35,080 --> 00:10:38,880
for your neighbor's children, but you're also helping in a practical

165
00:10:38,880 --> 00:10:44,560
fashion to bring to pass God's kingdom of peace and goodwill on earth.

166
00:10:45,120 --> 00:10:49,000
So, from my heart, I wish you Godspeed in your effort.

167
00:10:49,000 --> 00:10:53,240
I definitely couldn't say it any better than Beaton Powell.

168
00:10:53,440 --> 00:10:57,480
I hope that helps you, in these potentially divisive times,

169
00:10:58,080 --> 00:11:02,880
to think a little bit broader and hopefully, to address

170
00:11:02,880 --> 00:11:07,240
whatever concerns you may have and to unite us

171
00:11:07,720 --> 00:11:10,040
around the common things that we hold.

172
00:11:10,840 --> 00:11:13,440
We're going to have differences of politics,

173
00:11:13,840 --> 00:11:15,640
We're going to have differences of religion,

174
00:11:16,080 --> 00:11:18,560
We're going to have differences of custom and culture,

175
00:11:19,120 --> 00:11:22,320
But we can unite around scouting, can't we?

176
00:11:23,120 --> 00:11:25,960
So the remainder of this podcast we're going to spend answering

177
00:11:25,960 --> 00:11:27,600
a lot of email questions.

178
00:11:27,600 --> 00:11:30,960
I counted three or four or five, I guess, and they look like

179
00:11:31,200 --> 00:11:33,600
important questions that, I think, will help everybody out.

180
00:11:33,600 --> 00:11:36,120
So let's get started. shall we

181
00:11:37,000 --> 00:11:41,400
Write me a letter, send it my name

182
00:11:43,200 --> 00:11:45,480
Email? that is folks.

183
00:11:45,480 --> 00:11:48,440
And here's an answer to one of your emails,

184
00:11:50,000 --> 00:12:01,560
The first email question. I'm going to withhold the names

185
00:12:01,560 --> 00:12:03,760
and the identifying characteristics

186
00:12:03,760 --> 00:12:08,280
And you'll see why. I have a situation where my son is essentially

187
00:12:08,280 --> 00:12:10,840
being pushed out of scouts by his scout master.

188
00:12:11,200 --> 00:12:15,560
He is 15 and plays club soccer and high school soccer.

189
00:12:15,560 --> 00:12:19,960
He's currently a star scout and he is not being allowed to advance

190
00:12:19,960 --> 00:12:24,360
the life because he cannot fulfill his position of responsibility

191
00:12:24,360 --> 00:12:26,120
for six months straight.

192
00:12:27,360 --> 00:12:32,120
His scout master will only let him fulfill this position

193
00:12:32,120 --> 00:12:35,960
of responsibility by being a patrol leader when there are

194
00:12:35,960 --> 00:12:37,600
many other positions available

195
00:12:37,800 --> 00:12:40,520
And there's also the option for a special project.

196
00:12:40,880 --> 00:12:44,720
But the scout master is reading the position of responsibility

197
00:12:44,920 --> 00:12:46,160
as leadership.

198
00:12:47,040 --> 00:12:51,480
My son is basically in the position of choosing soccer or scouts,

199
00:12:52,200 --> 00:12:54,440
but he isn't welcome to do both.

200
00:12:54,440 --> 00:12:57,000
When you have scout masters who are unwilling to work with the

201
00:12:57,000 --> 00:13:00,640
scouts that have other interests besides scouting,

202
00:13:01,080 --> 00:13:03,000
that's when you lose a scout too.

203
00:13:03,000 --> 00:13:04,960
That's an upsetting message, isn't it?

204
00:13:04,960 --> 00:13:07,240
There are several issues that it suggests that.

205
00:13:07,520 --> 00:13:09,560
Let's see if we can unravel some of this

206
00:13:09,760 --> 00:13:12,520
In the star life and eagle requirements.

207
00:13:13,000 --> 00:13:16,360
you see the words position of responsibility

208
00:13:16,360 --> 00:13:20,400
a term for an office, whether elected or appointed,

209
00:13:20,760 --> 00:13:24,240
that a boy holds to qualify for those ranks.

210
00:13:24,680 --> 00:13:27,960
The words position of responsibility are carefully chosen

211
00:13:28,640 --> 00:13:32,160
because not every boy is a leader

212
00:13:33,120 --> 00:13:38,120
and not every boy will become a leader. quote unquote.

213
00:13:38,680 --> 00:13:43,560
Every scout, by taking out a position of responsibility,

214
00:13:43,560 --> 00:13:46,800
is certainly going to use some leadership skills

215
00:13:47,200 --> 00:13:49,960
and is certainly going to develop some leadership skills,

216
00:13:50,440 --> 00:13:54,440
But, quite wisely to my mind, we have divorced

217
00:13:54,880 --> 00:13:58,480
the term leadership from position of responsibility,

218
00:13:58,800 --> 00:14:02,920
because too many people use it to discourage-

219
00:14:03,240 --> 00:14:06,680
as is in the case of the person who sent me this email-

220
00:14:06,880 --> 00:14:08,760
rather than encourage scouts.

221
00:14:09,040 --> 00:14:12,040
So if we look at it from the standpoint of a position

222
00:14:12,040 --> 00:14:15,600
of responsibility and fulfilling those responsibilities,

223
00:14:15,800 --> 00:14:19,480
the intention of the requirement becomes much clearer, doesn't it?

224
00:14:19,840 --> 00:14:23,560
So remember, when evaluating whether or not

225
00:14:23,560 --> 00:14:26,240
a scout has fulfilled a position of responsibility,

226
00:14:26,560 --> 00:14:29,640
it's not whether or not he has fulfilled a leadership position,

227
00:14:29,640 --> 00:14:32,560
even though we use the terms interchangeably a lot.

228
00:14:32,560 --> 00:14:35,480
just, you know, as we hack around and we do scouting.

229
00:14:36,160 --> 00:14:38,760
But remember that that's what the requirement says:

230
00:14:38,760 --> 00:14:41,560
position of responsibility. OK,

231
00:14:41,840 --> 00:14:43,920
One of the other things we can kind of unravel here

232
00:14:43,920 --> 00:14:46,760
is this particular scout master's objection

233
00:14:46,760 --> 00:14:50,800
that the boy is not serving in a continuous fashion for six months.

234
00:14:51,200 --> 00:14:54,160
Well, if you go to the Guide to Advancement 2011,,

235
00:14:54,160 --> 00:14:58,320
you will find continuous service may not be required

236
00:14:58,320 --> 00:15:00,480
by the unit to qualify for a rank.

237
00:15:00,480 --> 00:15:03,600
If a boy is active for three months and then he's away for two,

238
00:15:03,600 --> 00:15:06,360
and then he's active for another two, and he's away for one,

239
00:15:06,720 --> 00:15:09,720
and he's active for another month in and then he's away for one,

240
00:15:09,720 --> 00:15:11,680
He's got his six months.

241
00:15:11,680 --> 00:15:13,960
So service in a position of responsibility

242
00:15:13,960 --> 00:15:16,240
does not have to be continuous.

243
00:15:16,240 --> 00:15:19,200
Then let's talk about active. OK,

244
00:15:19,200 --> 00:15:22,960
Because this scout master- and I didn't read you the entire email,

