00:15:31,120 --> 00:15:33,640
because he hasn't been to the troop standard.

249
00:15:33,960 --> 00:15:37,080
They've said a numerical standard of something like 75 percent

250
00:15:37,440 --> 00:15:40,320
of the meetings and 50 percent of the outings or something like that,

251
00:15:40,960 --> 00:15:43,240
And so he hasn't met that metric standard

252
00:15:43,240 --> 00:15:46,640
and the scout master considers that that's the end of the story.

253
00:15:46,640 --> 00:15:48,160
as far as active goes,

254
00:15:48,160 --> 00:15:50,720
Again, go to the Guide to Advancement,

255
00:15:51,080 --> 00:15:52,520
Go to section four.

256
00:15:52,520 --> 00:15:56,920
Take a look at how active is determined,

257
00:15:57,120 --> 00:15:59,400
because there's a very easy three step process.

258
00:15:59,400 --> 00:16:01,080
We've discussed this before.

259
00:16:01,080 --> 00:16:03,520
So step number one is he's registered.

260
00:16:03,520 --> 00:16:04,320
That's easy,

261
00:16:04,320 --> 00:16:06,200
That's just an administrative thing.

262
00:16:06,200 --> 00:16:07,520
He's a registered scout,

263
00:16:07,520 --> 00:16:08,680
That's all we need.

264
00:16:08,680 --> 00:16:10,920
Step number two: he's in good standing.

265
00:16:10,920 --> 00:16:14,120
and it's going to be extraordinarily rare

266
00:16:14,120 --> 00:16:15,600
that a scout is not in good standing

267
00:16:15,600 --> 00:16:17,920
because what that means is he's not been dismissed

268
00:16:17,920 --> 00:16:20,920
for disciplinary reasons or, for one way

269
00:16:20,920 --> 00:16:23,720
or one way or another, excluded from membership

270
00:16:23,720 --> 00:16:25,080
by the local council.

271
00:16:25,080 --> 00:16:28,800
And step number three is that if the troop establishes

272
00:16:28,800 --> 00:16:31,080
a metric standard- and yes, that's allowed,

273
00:16:31,080 --> 00:16:36,240
I wouldn't do it in a million years if it was me- OK,

274
00:16:36,240 --> 00:16:39,120
but some troops find that useful-

275
00:16:39,120 --> 00:16:41,520
If he meets the troops metric standard

276
00:16:41,520 --> 00:16:45,040
of whatever they decide- 75 percent or 50 percent

277
00:16:45,040 --> 00:16:48,560
or something like that- then he meets the requirements.

278
00:16:48,560 --> 00:16:50,960
If he doesn't meet that standard, though,

