they may be a little fuzzy

508
00:25:52,560 --> 00:25:54,120
and they may be difficult to find at times,

509
00:25:54,120 --> 00:25:56,600
but they're working because they lead us

510
00:25:56,600 --> 00:25:59,040
to think about what we're doing a little bit more

511
00:25:59,040 --> 00:26:00,439
and understanding the reasons

512
00:26:00,439 --> 00:26:02,200
that the rules are there in the first place

513
00:26:02,200 --> 00:26:04,320
and then applying the concepts behind them,

514
00:26:04,320 --> 00:26:07,520
And I would also note that the tour plan process

515
00:26:07,520 --> 00:26:09,580
is pretty good at making sure

516
00:26:09,580 --> 00:26:12,520
that we have the right kind of training prerequisites

517
00:26:12,520 --> 00:26:14,920
for the activities that we're planning.

518
00:26:14,920 --> 00:26:16,720
So if it passes muster there,

519
00:26:16,720 --> 00:26:18,160
I think that's a pretty good indication

520
00:26:18,160 --> 00:26:19,200
that you're good to go.

521
00:26:19,200 --> 00:26:20,320
You know there are a lot more rules

522
00:26:20,320 --> 00:26:21,440
and regulations out there now

523
00:26:21,440 --> 00:26:22,620
than there were 30 years ago

524
00:26:22,620 --> 00:26:25,360
when I first became an adult volunteer right,

525
00:26:25,360 --> 00:26:27,080
And whenever I look at them you know what.

526
00:26:27,080 --> 00:26:28,680
They seem to be pretty intelligent

527
00:26:28,680 --> 00:26:31,760
and they help us avoid putting scouts in harm's way

528
00:26:31,800 --> 00:26:34,480
and they focus us on the most effective parts of the program.

529
00:26:34,480 --> 00:26:36,160
So this question comes from Michael Kerry,

530
00:26:36,160 --> 00:26:39,080
who's the committee chair of Troop 167

531
00:26:39,080 --> 00:26:41,520
in Charlotte, North Carolina,

532
00:26:41,520 --> 00:26:44,080
And Michael emails me and says:

533
00:26:44,080 --> 00:26:45,520
Clark, I enjoy your podcast.

534
00:26:45,520 --> 00:26:46,560
Well, thank you, Michael.

535
00:26:46,560 --> 00:26:47,760
Always nice to hear that.

536
00:26:47,760 --> 00:26:50,240
Do any of your past podcasts

537
00:26:50,240 --> 00:26:53,400
discuss new scout patrols and their pros and cons?

538
00:26:53,400 --> 00:26:54,680
We currently don't have one,

539
00:26:54,680 --> 00:26:56,200
but the idea is being talked about

540
00:26:56,200 --> 00:26:59,040
and I'm looking for others past experiences.

541
00:26:59,040 --> 00:26:59,879
Thanks for your time.

542
00:26:59,879 --> 00:27:01,680
Well, thanks for being in touch, Mike.

543
00:27:01,720 --> 00:27:02,840
That's a great question.

544
00:27:02,840 --> 00:27:04,520
It's one that's been discussed in general,

545
00:27:04,520 --> 00:27:07,360
but I don't think really specifically on the podcast.

546
00:27:07,360 --> 00:27:09,120
So to answer it,

547
00:27:09,120 --> 00:27:12,120
we've really got to think about some basics about patrols.

548
00:27:12,120 --> 00:27:13,880
One of the most elemental things about scouting

549
00:27:13,880 --> 00:27:16,400
that we adults sometimes forget

550
00:27:16,400 --> 00:27:18,080
is that boys volunteer to be scouts

551
00:27:18,080 --> 00:27:20,040
so they can hang out with their friends and go camping.

552
00:27:20,040 --> 00:27:22,640
I mean, that's, you know, basically it

553
00:27:22,640 --> 00:27:26,840
They reduce that whole statement to. I want to have fun.

554
00:27:26,840 --> 00:27:29,500
In order to get at this question,

555
00:27:29,500 --> 00:27:31,080
I'm going to go back

556
00:27:31,080 --> 00:27:32,040
and I'm going to go back.

557
00:27:32,040 --> 00:27:34,560
Let's go all the way back to the founding

558
00:27:34,560 --> 00:27:36,720
of the scout movement and when it started.

559
00:27:36,720 --> 00:27:38,720
So bear with me for a moment.

560
00:27:38,720 --> 00:27:40,240
In the early part of the last century

561
00:27:40,240 --> 00:27:43,360
this new book appears- Scouting for Boys-

562
00:27:43,360 --> 00:27:45,639
And it shows up in the United States

563
00:27:45,639 --> 00:27:47,760
and it just starts to spread like wildfire.

564
00:27:47,760 --> 00:27:50,919
Boys everywhere are getting the book.

565
00:27:50,919 --> 00:27:52,840
They're getting a gang of their buddies together

566
00:27:52,840 --> 00:27:54,520
and they're forming patrols.

567
00:27:54,520 --> 00:27:56,240
They're becoming scouts.

568
00:27:56,240 --> 00:27:58,679
Nobody's telling them that they need to do this.

569
00:27:58,679 --> 00:28:00,480
You know adults aren't out looking for them

570
00:28:00,560 --> 00:28:02,680
and saying: we want you to be scouts.

571
00:28:02,680 --> 00:28:05,560
They just get the book and they're just so energized

572
00:28:05,560 --> 00:28:09,740
by the concept that they decide: I want to be a scout.

573
00:28:09,740 --> 00:28:13,240
So they make up a patrol and eventually the patrols

574
00:28:13,240 --> 00:28:15,720
you know are happening all over the country

575
00:28:15,720 --> 00:28:17,960
And soon there's patrols of scouts

576
00:28:17,960 --> 00:28:20,480
in every neighborhood, in every town

577
00:28:20,480 --> 00:28:22,120
And eventually they decide it would be fun

578
00:28:22,120 --> 00:28:23,640
to go camping with another patrol

579
00:28:23,640 --> 00:28:25,280
and they enlist the help of some adults

580
00:28:25,280 --> 00:28:28,200
and the idea of a scout troop comes about.

581
00:28:28,240 --> 00:28:31,880
And then that scout troop idea: well, we need some help.

582
00:28:31,880 --> 00:28:33,880
So we'll get together with the other troops in town

583
00:28:33,880 --> 00:28:36,240
and you understand where we're going.

584
00:28:36,240 --> 00:28:37,520
In a very short period of time

585
00:28:37,520 --> 00:28:40,320
we end up with a national administrative organization

586
00:28:40,320 --> 00:28:43,220
that's helping these boys do the things that they do.

587
00:28:43,220 --> 00:28:45,160
We go from there to what we have

588
00:28:45,160 --> 00:28:46,600
as the prevailing practice today

589
00:28:46,600 --> 00:28:49,640
Is that a boy, you know, joins a Cub Scout pack

590
00:28:49,640 --> 00:28:52,200
and he spends several years in a Cub Scout pack

591
00:28:52,200 --> 00:28:56,240
and then time comes for him to join a scout troop

592
00:28:56,240 --> 00:28:59,480
And so he transitions up into a scout troop

593
00:28:59,480 --> 00:29:01,680
and somebody puts him in a patrol,

594
00:29:01,680 --> 00:29:03,560
Just like they did when he was in a Cub Scout pack.

595
00:29:03,560 --> 00:29:05,440
you're in this den.

596
00:29:05,440 --> 00:29:07,640
Not a whole lot of choice there. you know,

597
00:29:07,640 --> 00:29:09,000
this is your den,

598
00:29:09,000 --> 00:29:11,920
And so a lot of times that's what we end up with

599
00:29:11,920 --> 00:29:13,320
at the scout troop level.

600
00:29:13,320 --> 00:29:15,680
We just repeat that practice and we say,

601
00:29:15,680 --> 00:29:17,940
well, you're gonna be in such and such patrol,

602
00:29:17,940 --> 00:29:20,560
the new scout patrol, or you're gonna be in this one,

603
00:29:20,560 --> 00:29:24,440
And that patrol may or may not be very important

604
00:29:24,440 --> 00:29:25,840
in the way the troop is administered,

605
00:29:25,840 --> 00:29:30,360
depending on how well the adults in the troop comprehend

606
00:29:30,360 --> 00:29:32,840
and understand the importance of patrols.

607
00:29:32,840 --> 00:29:35,880
Zoom out for a moment and look at our national organization,

608
00:29:35,880 --> 00:29:38,200
And our national organization is a great organization

609
00:29:38,200 --> 00:29:43,200
but it understands things on a very macro level

610
00:29:43,460 --> 00:29:46,880
And from a national standpoint. we know several things.

611
00:29:46,880 --> 00:29:51,200
One of the leading indicators is that we know

612
00:29:51,200 --> 00:29:54,240
scouts stay in scouting longer

613
00:29:54,240 --> 00:29:57,400
If they reach first class rank earlier,

614
00:29:57,400 --> 00:30:00,120
And so the rule of thumb is: we'd love to see them

615
00:30:00,120 --> 00:30:02,320
become first class rank in the first year.

616
00:30:03,660 --> 00:30:06,240
It just gets proven out by surveys and numbers

617
00:30:06,240 --> 00:30:07,480
and things like that.

618
00:30:07,480 --> 00:30:09,800
And we know that older scouts are supposed to be

619
00:30:11,200 --> 00:30:14,280
caring for and leading these younger scouts,

620
00:30:14,280 --> 00:30:15,960
but it doesn't always work in practice

621
00:30:15,960 --> 00:30:19,720
to the satisfaction of adults who are administering troops.

622
00:30:19,720 --> 00:30:24,720
And so you know we hear from adults mostly

623
00:30:24,800 --> 00:30:27,680
and we know that there are some people out there

624
00:30:27,680 --> 00:30:29,600
with promising practices and we look at one

625
00:30:29,600 --> 00:30:31,560
and it's this new scout patrol idea

626
00:30:32,640 --> 00:30:36,920
And that is where we have a group of new boys

627
00:30:36,920 --> 00:30:40,120
and we put them into the troop as a patrol

628
00:30:40,120 --> 00:30:44,000
and they get an older scout who's kind of their troop guide

629
00:30:44,000 --> 00:30:47,360
and then an adult also mentors that patrol

630
00:30:47,360 --> 00:30:50,080
And you know what. it looks great on paper

631
00:30:50,080 --> 00:30:52,120
And it works.

632
00:30:52,120 --> 00:30:54,680
If the troop is administered by adults

633
00:30:54,680 --> 00:30:57,960
and basically led by adults, it works pretty well

634
00:30:57,960 --> 00:30:59,960
And I've gotten really no argument.

635
00:30:59,960 --> 00:31:02,120
Boys have a great experience in troops

636
00:31:02,120 --> 00:31:03,400
that are administered by adults

637
00:31:03,400 --> 00:31:06,080
as well as they have in troops

638
00:31:06,080 --> 00:31:08,280
that are administered by youth.

639
00:31:08,280 --> 00:31:09,440
You know what?

640
00:31:09,440 --> 00:31:12,080
I can't really argue with the results that happen.

641
00:31:12,080 --> 00:31:15,400
I would say I would prefer that our troops

642
00:31:15,400 --> 00:31:16,360
were administered by youth,

643
00:31:16,400 --> 00:31:19,880
because I think that's what scouting actually is.

644
00:31:19,880 --> 00:31:21,760
But let's lay that aside for a moment.

645
00:31:21,760 --> 00:31:26,760
and we know that suggested practices that optimize

646
00:31:26,760 --> 00:31:30,600
the leading indicators are a good thing,

647
00:31:30,600 --> 00:31:33,960
And so we develop and promote this idea

648
00:31:33,960 --> 00:31:35,160
of a new scout patrol.

649
00:31:35,160 --> 00:31:38,600
Let's contrast what happened in the founding of scouting

650
00:31:38,600 --> 00:31:40,600
and what we're doing today. okay,

651
00:31:40,600 --> 00:31:42,680
We've got basically two practices

652
00:31:42,680 --> 00:31:45,480
and the founding years of scouting. boys

653
00:31:45,480 --> 00:31:48,160
are energized and interested in the concept.

654
00:31:48,160 --> 00:31:49,960
They form their own patrols

655
00:31:49,960 --> 00:31:53,600
And present practice is, in most cases,

656
00:31:53,600 --> 00:31:56,360
that decision is kind of an administrative one

657
00:31:56,360 --> 00:31:57,680
on the part of the troop.

658
00:31:57,680 --> 00:31:59,480
So, having gotten the case

659
00:31:59,480 --> 00:32:02,560
and contrasted those two things, I have an opinion.

660
00:32:02,560 --> 00:32:06,400
I amazing, right,

661
00:32:06,400 --> 00:32:07,920
I have an opinion about this.

662
00:32:07,920 --> 00:32:10,720
Well, anybody who's gonna take the time

663
00:32:10,720 --> 00:32:12,160
to stand here with a microphone

664
00:32:12,160 --> 00:32:13,760
and better have an opinion.

665
00:32:13,960 --> 00:32:15,400
I think scouts ought to be the ones

666
00:32:15,400 --> 00:32:17,400
to answer these questions,

667
00:32:17,400 --> 00:32:19,800
just like they did back when scouting

668
00:32:19,800 --> 00:32:22,440
was just beginning to get off the ground.

669
00:32:22,440 --> 00:32:24,480
When new scouts join a troop,

670
00:32:24,480 --> 00:32:25,720
I go to the senior patrol leader

671
00:32:25,720 --> 00:32:28,440
and I ask him what he'll be doing about this.

672
00:32:28,440 --> 00:32:30,360
He knows that they need to go into patrol

673
00:32:30,360 --> 00:32:32,640
and I'll say: how are you gonna do that?

674
00:32:32,640 --> 00:32:35,280
I said, well, he's already in whatever patrol

675
00:32:35,280 --> 00:32:37,240
And I'll say: sounds good to me

676
00:32:37,240 --> 00:32:39,920
and that'll be the end of the discussion.

677
00:32:39,920 --> 00:32:41,600
Nine times out of 10,

678
00:32:41,680 --> 00:32:43,320
a boy joining the troop

679
00:32:43,320 --> 00:32:45,280
who was not in a Weeblos den before

680
00:32:45,280 --> 00:32:47,840
already has a buddy in a patrol somewhere

681
00:32:47,840 --> 00:32:50,480
and that's just gonna work well.

682
00:32:50,480 --> 00:32:52,600
But what about that group of new Weeblos

683
00:32:52,600 --> 00:32:54,960
that are coming into the troop?

684
00:32:54,960 --> 00:32:56,720
Should we put them in a new scout patrol?

685
00:32:56,720 --> 00:32:58,120
Should we call it a new scout patrol?

686
00:32:58,120 --> 00:32:58,960
What do you wanna do?

687
00:32:58,960 --> 00:33:00,560
How do you wanna do it?

688
00:33:00,560 --> 00:33:03,240
Sometimes it works for them just to come in

689
00:33:03,240 --> 00:33:04,360
and be in all in one patrol.

690
00:33:04,360 --> 00:33:05,880
Sometimes they get split up.

691
00:33:06,880 --> 00:33:08,920
It really depends on what they want,

692
00:33:08,920 --> 00:33:12,280
because it's their volunteering to be part of this.

693
00:33:12,280 --> 00:33:13,680
Let them make a choice

694
00:33:13,680 --> 00:33:16,760
and let them change their minds, because they're boys

695
00:33:16,760 --> 00:33:19,160
and they need to change their minds all the time.

696
00:33:19,160 --> 00:33:20,520
What about balancing patrols?

697
00:33:20,520 --> 00:33:23,320
Shouldn't you have? if we have 24 boys in patrols,

698
00:33:23,320 --> 00:33:27,920
we should have patrols of eight guys apiece.

699
00:33:27,920 --> 00:33:29,320
And what about that?

700
00:33:29,320 --> 00:33:30,960
And well, you know what,

701
00:33:30,960 --> 00:33:32,360
From an administrative standpoint

702
00:33:32,360 --> 00:33:34,720
you'd like nice, even patrols, right.

703
00:33:34,720 --> 00:33:37,200
But from a boy standpoint, do they really care?

704
00:33:37,680 --> 00:33:41,600
You know, I would love to see them build a patrol

705
00:33:41,600 --> 00:33:42,520
up to a strength of eight,

706
00:33:42,520 --> 00:33:44,560
but if there's five guys in a patrol

707
00:33:44,560 --> 00:33:46,440
and that's what they like

708
00:33:46,440 --> 00:33:48,520
and that's working for them,

709
00:33:48,520 --> 00:33:50,040
who am I gonna be to come in and say:

710
00:33:50,040 --> 00:33:52,880
we gotta even the numbers up here. okay,

711
00:33:52,880 --> 00:33:54,720
If they've got 10 guys in one patrol

712
00:33:54,720 --> 00:33:56,360
and five guys in another patrol

713
00:33:56,360 --> 00:33:58,520
and three guys in a patrol,

714
00:33:59,360 --> 00:34:01,600
it's not what I would call optimum,

715
00:34:01,600 --> 00:34:05,560
but if it's working, why do I wanna stir the pot?

716
00:34:05,560 --> 00:34:07,280
Why do I wanna mess with that?

717
00:34:07,280 --> 00:34:10,000
Being able to do this presupposes another thing.

718
00:34:10,000 --> 00:34:11,400
It kind of pulls on another thread

719
00:34:11,400 --> 00:34:12,480
and that's youth leadership.

720
00:34:12,480 --> 00:34:14,679
Now, if the youth of the troop,

721
00:34:14,679 --> 00:34:17,759
if the youth in that scout troop,

722
00:34:17,759 --> 00:34:21,440
have actual responsibility to take care of things,

723
00:34:21,440 --> 00:34:23,000
if they're actually leading

724
00:34:23,000 --> 00:34:24,880
and they're not just figureheads,

725
00:34:24,880 --> 00:34:27,840
then they can make these decisions pretty well

726
00:34:27,840 --> 00:34:31,080
If they've been trained to lead

727
00:34:31,080 --> 00:34:33,279
and they've been inculcated with the concept

728
00:34:33,280 --> 00:34:35,880
that they are to care for, support

729
00:34:35,880 --> 00:34:38,920
and be a big brother to younger scouts,

730
00:34:38,920 --> 00:34:42,040
that these are not just little, bothersome little kids

731
00:34:42,040 --> 00:34:45,000
that are just getting in their way

732
00:34:45,000 --> 00:34:49,040
And they have a free hand in making the kinds of decisions

733
00:34:49,040 --> 00:34:53,080
about who's in what patrol and things like that.

734
00:34:53,080 --> 00:34:55,360
I think that the quality of their decisions

735
00:34:55,360 --> 00:34:57,520
will be better than those based on

736
00:34:57,520 --> 00:35:00,320
kind of administrative concerns and things.

737
00:35:00,320 --> 00:35:01,560
Perhaps you would like me to tell you

738
00:35:01,560 --> 00:35:02,640
one way or the other what to do,

739
00:35:02,640 --> 00:35:05,240
but that gives you some food for thought

740
00:35:05,240 --> 00:35:06,960
as you sit and make that decision.

741
00:35:08,440 --> 00:35:10,319
In my book, let the boys choose.

742
00:35:10,319 --> 00:35:12,160
they make better decisions anyway.

743
00:35:12,160 --> 00:35:14,160
That's why they're in the troop in the first place,

744
00:35:14,160 --> 00:35:15,720
because they want to be with their buddies.

745
00:35:15,720 --> 00:35:17,560
If a new group comes in

746
00:35:17,560 --> 00:35:19,600
and it would be useful for them

747
00:35:19,600 --> 00:35:21,799
to have an older scout working with them,

748
00:35:21,799 --> 00:35:24,920
then let the senior patrol leader make that decision right

749
00:35:24,920 --> 00:35:27,600
And monitor and advise and mentor

750
00:35:27,600 --> 00:35:29,759
and do all the things that we always talk about right.

751
00:35:29,759 --> 00:35:31,600
But, Michael, I appreciate the question

752
00:35:31,640 --> 00:35:33,319
and let me know if I can explain it better

753
00:35:33,319 --> 00:35:35,279
or be of any further assistance.

754
00:35:35,279 --> 00:35:38,279
["The Scoutmaster Podcast"].

